SUMMARY:Arts Multilingual Week (Oct 26–Nov 19)
DESCRIPTION:AMW 2026 is the perfect opportunity to immerse yourself in cultures and languages from around the world and celebrate multilingualism at UBC V! \nIn collaboration with multiple units from the Faculty of Arts and beyond\, our program will showcase a wide array of student-focused activities aimed at engaging with the rich tapestry of languages spoken across campus. \nHighlights include a Multilingual Poetry Slam (Nov. 4)\, the Speech Contest on Translation\, Language Learning & AI (Nov. 5)\, lively Karaoke (Nov. 4) and a Multilingual Open Mic Nights (Nov. 5) at The Gallery in the Nest\, and much more! \nJoin us for prizes\, free food\, and fun! \nAre You interested in participating in Arts Multilingual Week 2026? Register here to attend\, participate in\, and volunteer for our various events. Then\, follow us on Instagram here\, and check out multilingualweek.arts.ubc.ca for more information. \n 
URL:https://events.ubc.ca/event/arts-multilingual-week-oct-26-nov-19/
LOCATION:Forest Engineering Research Institute of Canada (FERIC)\, 2601 East Mall\, Vancouver\, British Columbia\, V6T1Z2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Audience – All Students,Audience – Community,Audience – Undergraduate Students,Subject – Entertainment – Arts,Subject – Entertainment – Culture,Subject – Entertainment – Music,Subject – Entertainment – Social,Subject – Equity, Diversity and Inclusion,Subject – Learning And Research – Arts, Humanities And Social Sciences,Subject – Learning And Research – Community,Type – Film
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.ubc.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/AMW-2026-Flyer-Fall-2025.png
END:VEVENT
