SUMMARY:UBC CPD: Nawh Whu’nus’en - We See in Two Worlds: Trauma sensitive practices for collectively healing in relationship Level 1 (Nov 3)
DESCRIPTION:Note: this edition of Nawh Whu’nus’en Level 1 is restricted to physicians only.  \nThe Nawh Whu’nus’en – We See in Two Worlds Level 1 Workshop is based on a widely accepted understanding that trauma-sensitive practices are the basis for offering culturally-safe and respectful health services for Indigenous relatives. It draws upon two-eyed seeing models\, weaving together Indigenous ways of knowing with western trauma theory and neuroscience. The curriculum recognizes that health professionals and patients work in relationship\, and a trauma-sensitive approach can help to build respectful\, trusting relationships. Participants also reflect on their own experiences of trauma and ways to support their own wellness.
URL:https://events.ubc.ca/event/ubc-cpd-nawh-whunusen-we-see-in-two-worlds-trauma-sensitive-practices-for-collectively-healing-in-relationship-level-1-nov-3/
LOCATION:Online/Virtual Event
CATEGORIES:Subject – Personal And Professional Development – Faculty
