SUMMARY:CGRS M: Crafting a Compelling Research Story
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is designed for students applying for the Canada Graduate Research Scholarship – Master’s (CGRS M). Drawing on evidence-based research about successful grant proposals\, the facilitator discusses particular elements of this written academic genre: audience\, purpose\, knowledge gap\, competence claim\, structure\, style\, and more. The workshop includes examples of successful UBC CGRS M research proposals\, as well as dedicated time to write in community. \nFacilitator: Dr. Xuan Zhang\, Centre for Writing and Scholarly Communication \nLocation: IKBLC\, Level 3\, Dodson Room and on Zoom. Registrants receive the Zoom link 1 day prior to the workshop.
URL:https://events.ubc.ca/event/cgrs-m-crafting-a-compelling-research-story/
LOCATION:Hybrid Online/Virtual and In-Person – See Description\, Vancouver\, British Columbia\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Audience – Graduate Students,Audience – Undergraduate Students,Subject – Personal And Professional Development – Students,Type – Workshop
