SUMMARY:UBC x Jade Music Fest 2026 | Panel Discussion: Who Gets Heard?
DESCRIPTION:Join UBC Hong Kong Studies Initiative and Jade Music Fest for “Who Gets Heard?”\, a panel discussion exploring language\, accents\, and meaningful representation for artists in Canada. Featuring Vancouver-based music artists Caroline Ding\, Daniel Lew\, and hip-hop artist Scope G alongside CreativeBC’s Joseph Bardsley\, moderated by Dr. Helena Wu (UBC Department of Asian Studies). \nDate: Wed\, 04 November 2026\nTime: 12:00 – 14:15\nVenue: Coach House\, Green College\, UBC \nThe event will be conducted in English; free admission with registration: https://hksi.ubc.ca/events/event/jmf2026_panel/
